# Angular Client App Cursor Rules

## Technology Stack
- Angular 19.x with SSR
- TypeScript 5.5
- SCSS for styling
- Jest for testing
- Akita for state management (legacy)
- Angular Signals (preferred for new code)

## Component Development

### Standalone Component Template
```typescript
import {
  ChangeDetectionStrategy,
  Component,
  EventEmitter,
  inject,
  Input,
  Output,
  signal,
  ViewEncapsulation,
} from '@angular/core';
import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';

@Component({
  selector: 'feature-component-name',
  imports: [CommonModule],
  templateUrl: './component.component.html',
  styleUrl: './component.component.scss',
  encapsulation: ViewEncapsulation.ShadowDom,
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
})
export class ComponentNameComponent {
  @Input() inputProperty: Type | null = null;
  @Output() outputEvent = new EventEmitter<Type>();

  // Use signals for internal state
  internalState = signal<Type>(defaultValue);

  // Inject dependencies using inject()
  private service = inject(ServiceName);
}
```

### Component File Structure
Each component should have these files:
- `component-name.component.ts` - Component logic
- `component-name.component.html` - Template
- `component-name.component.scss` - Styles
- `component-name.component.spec.ts` - Tests
- `index.ts` - Export file

### Event Handling Patterns
```typescript
// DOM Event Listeners with Cleanup
export class ComponentWithEvents implements OnDestroy {
  private eventCleanup: (() => void)[] = [];

  ngOnDestroy() {
    this.eventCleanup.forEach(cleanup => cleanup());
  }

  private addEventListeners() {
    const handleClick = (event: MouseEvent) => {
      // Handle click
    };

    document.addEventListener('click', handleClick);
    this.eventCleanup.push(() =>
      document.removeEventListener('click', handleClick)
    );
  }
}
```

## State Management

### Signal-based Store Pattern
```typescript
import { Injectable, signal } from '@angular/core';
import { IDataType } from '../types';

@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class FeatureStore {
  // Private signals for mutable state
  private _data = signal<IDataType[]>([]);
  private _loading = signal<boolean>(false);

  // Public readonly access
  readonly data = this._data.asReadonly();
  readonly loading = this._loading.asReadonly();

  // Actions
  setLoading(loading: boolean) {
    this._loading.set(loading);
  }

  updateData(newData: IDataType) {
    this._data.update(current => [...current, newData]);
  }

  removeData(id: string) {
    this._data.update(current =>
      current.filter(item => item.id !== id)
    );
  }
}
```

## Service Development

### Service Template
```typescript
import { Injectable, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';
import { Observable } from 'rxjs';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root'
})
export class FeatureService {
  private http = inject(HttpClient);

  getData(): Observable<DataType[]> {
    return this.http.get<DataType[]>('/api/data');
  }
}
```

## Type Definitions

### Interface Naming and Structure
```typescript
// Use I prefix for interfaces
export interface ICell {
  value: string | number | null;
  formula?: string;
  computedValue?: string | number | null;
  styles?: ICellStyles;
}

// Export type aliases for reusability
export type CellValue = ICell['value'];

// Use Record for key-value mappings
export interface ISheet {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  cells: Record<string, ICell>; // key-value mapping
}
```

## Routing

### Feature Route Configuration
```typescript
// features/feature-name/feature-name.route.ts
import { Routes } from '@angular/router';
import { FeatureComponent } from './components/feature/feature.component';

export const featureRoutes: Routes = [
  {
    path: '',
    component: FeatureComponent,
  },
  {
    path: 'sub-route',
    component: SubComponent,
  }
];
```

### Main Route Integration
```typescript
// app.routes.ts
export const routes: Routes = [
  {
    path: 'feature',
    loadChildren: () =>
      import('./features/feature/feature.module').then(
        (m) => m.FeatureModule
      ),
  },
];
```

## Testing

### Component Test Template
```typescript
import { ComponentFixture, TestBed } from '@angular/core/testing';
import { ComponentName } from './component-name.component';

describe('ComponentName', () => {
  let component: ComponentName;
  let fixture: ComponentFixture<ComponentName>;

  beforeEach(async () => {
    await TestBed.configureTestingModule({
      imports: [ComponentName] // For standalone components
    }).compileComponents();

    fixture = TestBed.createComponent(ComponentName);
    component = fixture.componentInstance;
    fixture.detectChanges();
  });

  it('should create', () => {
    expect(component).toBeTruthy();
  });
});
```

### Service Test Template
```typescript
import { TestBed } from '@angular/core/testing';
import { ServiceName } from './service-name.service';

describe('ServiceName', () => {
  let service: ServiceName;

  beforeEach(() => {
    TestBed.configureTestingModule({});
    service = TestBed.inject(ServiceName);
  });

  it('should be created', () => {
    expect(service).toBeTruthy();
  });
});
```

## File Path Patterns

### Import Aliases
- `@core/*` maps to `src/app/core/*`
- Use relative imports within the same feature
- Use absolute imports for cross-feature dependencies

### Directory Structure
```
src/app/
├── core/
│   ├── services/
│   │   └── auth/
│   │       ├── auth.service.ts
│   │       ├── auth.service.spec.ts
│   │       └── index.ts
│   └── core.config.ts
├── features/
│   └── editor/
│       ├── components/
│       │   ├── cell/
│       │   │   ├── cell.component.ts
│       │   │   ├── cell.component.html
│       │   │   ├── cell.component.scss
│       │   │   ├── cell.component.spec.ts
│       │   │   └── index.ts
│       │   └── editor/
│       ├── store/
│       │   ├── editor.store.ts
│       │   └── index.ts
│       ├── types.ts
│       ├── editor.module.ts
│       └── editor.route.ts
└── shared/
    └── types/
```

## Styling Guidelines

### SCSS Structure
```scss
// component.component.scss
:host {
  display: block;

  .component-wrapper {
    // Component-specific styles
  }

  &.modifier-class {
    // Modifier styles
  }
}

// Use CSS custom properties for theming
:host {
  --primary-color: #007bff;
  --secondary-color: #6c757d;
}
```

### Shadow DOM Styling
- Use `:host` selector for component root
- Use CSS custom properties for theme variables
- Avoid global style dependencies

## Performance Guidelines

### Change Detection
- Always use `OnPush` change detection strategy
- Use signals to trigger change detection efficiently
- Minimize unnecessary re-renders

### Memory Management
- Implement `OnDestroy` for cleanup
- Remove event listeners in `ngOnDestroy`
- Unsubscribe from observables when using RxJS

### Bundle Optimization
- Use lazy loading for feature modules
- Implement tree-shaking friendly imports
- Avoid importing entire libraries when only specific functions are needed

## Code Quality

### TypeScript Best Practices
- Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json
- Avoid `any` type - use proper typing
- Use type guards for runtime type checking
- Prefer interfaces over types for object shapes

### Error Handling
```typescript
// Service error handling
import { catchError, throwError } from 'rxjs';

getData(): Observable<DataType[]> {
  return this.http.get<DataType[]>('/api/data').pipe(
    catchError(error => {
      console.error('API Error:', error);
      return throwError(() => new Error('Failed to fetch data'));
    })
  );
}
```

## Development Workflow

### New Component Checklist
1. Create component folder in appropriate feature
2. Generate component files (ts, html, scss, spec.ts)
3. Add to index.ts export
4. Write basic tests
5. Add to module imports if using modules
6. Update types.ts if new interfaces are needed

### New Feature Checklist
1. Create feature folder under `src/app/features/`
2. Set up component structure
3. Create feature module and routes
4. Add store/state management
5. Define types in types.ts
6. Add feature route to main routes
7. Write comprehensive tests
